div.p:
The United States of America and His Majesty the King of Great Britain and Ireland and of the British Dominions Beyond the Seas, Emperor of India, being desirous of suppressing smuggling operations along the boundary between the Dominion of Canada and the United States, and of assisting in the arrest and prosecution of persons violating the customs, liquor, and narcotic laws of either government, have agreed to conclude a convention to give effect to these purposes and have named as their plenipotentiaries:
The President of the United States, . . . . . . . ;
His Britannic Majesty, . . . . . . . ;
